{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And these are the garments, etc. — all of them are explicitly explained ahead of us." "חשן — according to its context and plain sense, like a sheath or pouch, for it was doubled." "ואפוד — a term for a garment with which people adorn themselves and by which a person is covered above all his garments." "משבצות — it is made in the manner of hollows, hollow after hollow." "מצנפת — a cap on the head, as written: וְצְנִיף מְלוּכָה." "And the sash — a girdle, by the plain sense. There was no need to mention breeches here, for he mentions only garments that are visible, made for honor."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:23.952211477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}